{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A bill of severance.</b> A bill of severance [of divorce]." "<b>Your mother.</b> And [it is] between him and his wife. Now this would contradict the words of Jeremiah: \"and I gave her a bill of severance\" (Jeremiah 3:8). The answer is that Jeremiah spoke about the kingdom of Israel, which will never rise again, and likewise \"it will not rise again\" (Amos 8:2), while Isaiah spoke about the kingdom of David, from whom the Messiah will come."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:50.270966894Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}